('127.297.d.4.A',4,'A sports shoe brand aims its new line at teen athletes instead of all shoppers. This choice defines its:','["Product life cycle", "Target market", "Distribution channel", "Break-even point"]'::jsonb,1,'Choosing a specific customer group defines the target market.','original'),
('127.297.d.4.B',4,'A retailer creates separate ads for students, parents, and retirees. A cost of doing this is that:','["Data becomes unnecessary", "Customers are ignored", "Each segment needs its own message, which raises planning expense", "Only one ad is needed"]'::jsonb,2,'Multiple segments multiply planning and production costs.','original')
